            ],
            "tests": [
                {
                    "time_span": {
                        "start": 0,
                        "end": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": "tvd_monotone",
                    "assertions": [
                        {
                            "expected": 0.25,
                            "time": 0,
                            "reduce": "mean",
                            "variable": "u",
                            "tolerance": {
                                "abs": 1.0e-9
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "expected": 0.25,
                            "time": 0.5,
                            "reduce": "mean",
                            "variable": "u",
                            "tolerance": {
                                "abs": 1.0e-9
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "expected": 0.87,
                            "time": 0.5,
                            "reduce": "max",
                            "variable": "u",
                            "tolerance": {
                                "abs": 0.12
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "expected": 0.035,
                            "time": 0.5,
                            "reduce": "min",
                            "variable": "u",
                            "tolerance": {
                                "abs": 0.065
                            }
                        }
                    ],
                    "description": "Monotonicity / TVD gate: the tent u0(x) = max(0, 1 - 4|x - 1/2|) (max 1, min 0, mean 1/4) advected at c=1 to t=0.5. Assert (all STATE reductions, the sim-expressible form of the TVD claim): mean = 1/4 to machine precision at t=0 and t=0.5 (exact conservation of the flux-difference form); max(u) <= the no-overshoot bound at t=0.5 (a dispersive scheme would exceed 1); min(u) >= the no-undershoot bound at t=0.5 (a non-TVD scheme undershoots below 0). Bands de-risked in numpy at N=64."
                }
            ]
        }
    },
    "metadata": {
        "name": "advection_1d_periodic_minmod_tvd",
        "references": [
            {
                "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2002). Finite Volume Methods for Hyperbolic Problems. Cambridge University Press. Chapter 6 (TVD / total-variation-diminishing methods)."
            },
            {
                "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(83)90136-5",
                "citation": "Harten, A. (1983). High resolution schemes for hyperbolic conservation laws. J. Comput. Phys. 49(3):357-393 (TVD property)."
            }
        ],
        "tags": [
            "esd:problem",
            "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
            "equation:advection",
            "monotonicity"
        ],
        "license": "MIT",
        "description": "Monotonicity / TVD driver for grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/flux_limiter_minmod_D_periodic (minmod flux limiter (second-order TVD)) on the periodic unit interval [0,1], c = 1. A piecewise-linear tent profile u0(x) = max(0, 1 - 4|x - 1/2|) (peak 1 at x=1/2, min 0, mean 1/4; zero at the domain edges so the periodic wrap carries no seam) is advected to t=0.5. A TVD / monotonicity-preserving scheme develops NO new extrema (total variation non-increasing): it neither overshoots above the initial maximum (max stays under ~0.99, whereas a dispersive/non-TVD scheme would exceed 1) nor undershoots below the initial minimum (min stays >= -0.03; a non-TVD central scheme undershoots to about -0.04 on this profile), and the flux-difference form conserves the mean EXACTLY (1/4 to machine precision). Because the assertion evaluator cannot evaluate a state-dependent observed at assertion time, the gate drives the STATE and asserts REDUCTIONS of the state directly (max/min bounds + mean conservation), never an observed of the operator output — the sim-expressible form of the monotonicity claim. De-risked in numpy at N=64, t=0.5: this scheme's max/min/mean sit inside the asserted bands with comfortable margin. The grid geometry contract is fulfilled for [0,1] (x0 = 0, dx = 1/N); the tent ic is spelled inline from literals and N (build-time cellwise evaluation is scope-free). Companion MMS accuracy driver: problems/advection_1d_periodic_minmod.esm."
    }
}